Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix: v0.43 sheet wiring, round 1 (roll and link actions
 as plain builders; settle types in the hooks' types.ts)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The review of commit 17 (U1-m2): the pane's useRollActions and useDescriptionLinks call no React
hook; they build per-render closures, as the pane did inline. CLAUDE.md §3 asks for no hook where
React isn't needed, so they are plain functions now: rollActions (character-pane/roll-actions.ts)
and linkActions (character-pane/link-actions.ts, named apart from the DescriptionLinks component
and utils/description-links). Same arguments, same object, same call places in RollingSheet; no
React Compiler is configured, so nothing compiles differently.

U1-m4: Settling, SettleOptions, Settle and Spending are read only by src/features/sheet/hooks
(use-settle, use-spent-set, use-spent-removals), so they move from the feature's types.ts to
src/features/sheet/hooks/types.ts (§1.0 rule 3, the narrowest folder). Type-only; the feature's
types.ts keeps Belonging.

No string, request, id, attribute or effect order changes; eslint over the changed files prints
nothing; L0 and L1 as the report says.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
